<title>USA: SFX Broadcasting buys stations for $35 mln.</title>
<headline>SFX Broadcasting buys stations for $35 mln.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>SFX Broadcasting Inc said on Tuesday that it has agreed to acquire WVTY-FM, WTAE-AM in Pittsburgh and WLTQ-FM, WISN-AM in Milwaukee from Hearst Broadcasting Group for $35 million.</p>
<p>The company said in a release that WVTY and WTAE give it immediate and identifiable ratings and revenue opportunities in a new demographic cluster.</p>
<p>With the anticipated consummation of all previously announced transactions, SFX will own and operate or provide services to 80 stations in 23 markets, the company said.</p>
</text>
